omx-clap-host (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * clap_host_limits.h: the extra-inputs refusal comment matches the
    contract's wording
  * Version 0.7.0: the transport, side-chain and meter calls get their own
    version node
  * lv2 tests: lv2_asan_test carries the licence header the other tests have
  * lv2: a bundle stays loaded when its last reference goes
  * core: the meter kinds under the library's own names, for a consumer
    without clap_meters.h (FreeMixer/openmixer#1585)
  * core: an instance's clap.meters/1, read through
    omx_clap_host_meter_count, _info and _values (FreeMixer/openmixer#1585)
  * docs: a program hosting in process reads clap.meters/1 through the
    library (FreeMixer/openmixer#1585)
  * lv2: the kinds check's comments say every stage-2 kind now has its
    fixture (#48)
  * ci: run the stage-2 kinds check in the test job
  * lv2: the stage-2 kinds check also fails when its exit status is lost
  * lv2: a check names which stage-2 kinds have no fixture
  * lv2 tests: each side-chain fixture group has the lv2:symbol port-groups
    asks for (#48)
  * core: the auxiliary inputs' process list follows the instance's fields,
    so no field of the stage moves (#48)
  * core: a bound auxiliary pair carries its length, and no block reads past
    it (#48)
  * docs: LV2 matrix rows for side chains and port groups
  * lv2: side chains are CLAP inputs, port groups read
  * core: admit auxiliary inputs, fed silence until bound
  * lv2 clap test: line-buffered output, so a run that stops names its last
    check (#48)
  * core: omx_clap_host_set_transport goes in a 0.5 version node, not the
    released 0.4 (#48)
  * Write the bar comment in the present tense
  * LV2 adapter: forge time:Position from the host's transport
  * Document the fields of the published transport for make docs
  * Hand the plugin the host's whole transport, not only the tempo
  * packaging: the RPM check builds with libasan, which test-lv2 now links
    (#48)
  * lv2/core: append a MIDI event through the buffer's bytes, which GCC's LTO
    does not read as an overflow (#48)
  * lv2/clap: say how long an output sysex's bytes stay valid (#48)
  * lv2 tests: the MIDI output path runs under AddressSanitizer
  * lv2/core: refuse a MIDI message bigger than its buffer before padding it
  * lv2 tests: a MIDI output sequence in beats passes nothing
  * lv2/clap: map MIDI through clap.note-ports and the event lists
  * lv2/core: carry MIDI messages through the atom buffers of the MIDI ports
  * lv2/core: read a MIDI atom port as the MIDI input or output
  * lv2: the patch type starts initialised, which GCC's LTO cannot prove
    otherwise (#48)
  * lv2: a patch parameter is typed lv2:Parameter, the class LV2 defines (#48)
  * docs: the patch row names the CLAP face's test (#48)
  * lv2 clap test: the patch parameters through the face
  * lv2 patch test: a value the plugin emits on its own is kept
  * docs: the compatibility matrix's numeric patch row
  * lv2 shim: numeric patch properties as CLAP parameters
  * lv2: numeric patch properties through a patch port
  * lv2: refuse a state longer than 1 MiB on load (#48)
  * docs: a state longer than 1 MiB is refused (#48)
  * lv2: load a pset:Preset through clap.preset-load
  * lv2: save and restore the state through clap.state
  * lv2: refuse state:mapPath and state:makePath in the fixture, as the twins
    prove
  * lv2 clap test: line-buffered output, so a run that stops names its last
    check (#48)
  * Version 0.5.0: the host's whole transport reaches the plugins (#48)
  * core: omx_clap_host_set_transport goes in a 0.5 version node, not the
    released 0.4 (#48)
